  25685,321:           "description": "I've hit a snag with TypeScript. Specifically, I'm wrestling with an inferred type issue where `markdown` is incorrectly identified. The type is `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`, I need to adjust type guards to ensure I'm not running into an `external` error, because of how I'm handling the `remote` condition in my code.",
  25704,230:             "summary": "I'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 500 to investigate why TypeScript is failing to correctly narrow the type of `markdown`. It seems that my previous `if (markdown.kind === 'remote')` check is causing `markdown` to be inferred as only `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`, making the subsequent `external` check appear invalid. I'll refactor the type narrowing logic to explicitly handle all agent kinds, resolving the \"no overlap\" and \"property does not exist\" errors. This is necessary for a successful build and the final TASK-06 implementation.",
  25713,305:                   "output": "Current topic: \"Resolving Agent Loader Type Issues\"\nTopic summary: I'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 500 to investigate why TypeScript is failing to correctly narrow the type of `markdown`. It seems that my previous `if (markdown.kind === 'remote')` check is causing `markdown` to be inferred as only `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`, making the subsequent `external` check appear invalid. I'll refactor the type narrowing logic to explicitly handle all agent kinds, resolving the \"no overlap\" and \"property does not exist\" errors. This is necessary for a successful build and the final TASK-06 implementation.\n\nStrategic Intent: Fixing TypeScript errors in AgentLoader.ts."
  25720,303:           "resultDisplay": "## 📂 Topic: **Resolving Agent Loader Type Issues**\n\n**Summary:**\nI'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 500 to investigate why TypeScript is failing to correctly narrow the type of `markdown`. It seems that my previous `if (markdown.kind === 'remote')` check is causing `markdown` to be inferred as only `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`, making the subsequent `external` check appear invalid. I'll refactor the type narrowing logic to explicitly handle all agent kinds, resolving the \"no overlap\" and \"property does not exist\" errors. This is necessary for a successful build and the final TASK-06 implementation.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Fixing TypeScript errors in AgentLoader.ts.",
  25831,125:           "description": "I'm wrestling with how TypeScript infers types. It seems to assume that if `markdown.kind` isn't 'remote', then it *must* be `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`. This is wrong because `FrontmatterAgentDefinition` is a union, including local, remote, and other possibilities. I need to figure out why this inference is happening.",
  25831,267:           "description": "I'm wrestling with how TypeScript infers types. It seems to assume that if `markdown.kind` isn't 'remote', then it *must* be `FrontmatterLocalAgentDefinition`. This is wrong because `FrontmatterAgentDefinition` is a union, including local, remote, and other possibilities. I need to figure out why this inference is happening.",
  25912,222:           "description": "I'm making progress clarifying how the union type works with `z.union`. I've realized that the order of checks might be causing issues when trying to narrow the type. Specifically, checking for 'remote' first seems to prevent proper type narrowing in subsequent checks. The `system_prompt` field's absence in `FrontmatterExternalAgentDefinition` is causing a TS error, indicating incorrect type narrowing.",
  25931,301:             "summary": "I'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 200 to re-verify the `FrontmatterAgentDefinition` union type. I suspect that the way it's defined, or the surrounding code, is causing TypeScript to incorrectly narrow `markdown.kind` to `\"local\"` after the `remote` check. I'll check if `FrontmatterExternalAgentDefinition` was correctly added to the union and ensure that all agent kinds are properly represented. This will help me resolve the \"no overlap\" error and provide a type-safe loading path for external agents.",
  25940,380:                   "output": "Current topic: \"Verifying Agent Frontmatter Union Type\"\nTopic summary: I'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 200 to re-verify the `FrontmatterAgentDefinition` union type. I suspect that the way it's defined, or the surrounding code, is causing TypeScript to incorrectly narrow `markdown.kind` to `\"local\"` after the `remote` check. I'll check if `FrontmatterExternalAgentDefinition` was correctly added to the union and ensure that all agent kinds are properly represented. This will help me resolve the \"no overlap\" error and provide a type-safe loading path for external agents.\n\nStrategic Intent: Re-evaluating agent frontmatter type definitions."
  25947,378:           "resultDisplay": "## 📂 Topic: **Verifying Agent Frontmatter Union Type**\n\n**Summary:**\nI'm reading `packages/core/src/agents/agentLoader.ts` around line 200 to re-verify the `FrontmatterAgentDefinition` union type. I suspect that the way it's defined, or the surrounding code, is causing TypeScript to incorrectly narrow `markdown.kind` to `\"local\"` after the `remote` check. I'll check if `FrontmatterExternalAgentDefinition` was correctly added to the union and ensure that all agent kinds are properly represented. This will help me resolve the \"no overlap\" error and provide a type-safe loading path for external agents.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Re-evaluating agent frontmatter type definitions.",
