  29200,132:           "description": "I'm currently reviewing the changes to `AgentRegistry.registerAgent`. I see it only handles `local` and `remote` agents. I need to update it to accommodate the `external` agent type as well. Once that's settled, I can confidently update the unit test for `getAllDefinitions()`.",
  29218,405:             "summary": "I've discovered that `AgentRegistry.registerAgent` in `packages/core/src/agents/registry.ts` is missing explicit support for the `external` agent kind. I'm updating the method to recognize `external` agents and call a new `registerExternalAgent` method. This new method will handle basic validation and add the agent to the internal registry, mirroring the behavior for local and remote agents. This is a critical fix for ensuring that external agents discovered by the loader are actually registered and available for orchestration in Gemini CLI teams.",
  29228,487:                   "output": "Current topic: \"Integrating External Agents into Registry\"\nTopic summary: I've discovered that `AgentRegistry.registerAgent` in `packages/core/src/agents/registry.ts` is missing explicit support for the `external` agent kind. I'm updating the method to recognize `external` agents and call a new `registerExternalAgent` method. This new method will handle basic validation and add the agent to the internal registry, mirroring the behavior for local and remote agents. This is a critical fix for ensuring that external agents discovered by the loader are actually registered and available for orchestration in Gemini CLI teams.\n\nStrategic Intent: Adding external agent support to AgentRegistry."
  29235,485:           "resultDisplay": "## 📂 Topic: **Integrating External Agents into Registry**\n\n**Summary:**\nI've discovered that `AgentRegistry.registerAgent` in `packages/core/src/agents/registry.ts` is missing explicit support for the `external` agent kind. I'm updating the method to recognize `external` agents and call a new `registerExternalAgent` method. This new method will handle basic validation and add the agent to the internal registry, mirroring the behavior for local and remote agents. This is a critical fix for ensuring that external agents discovered by the loader are actually registered and available for orchestration in Gemini CLI teams.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Adding external agent support to AgentRegistry.",
